From: sie-mcp web <web@sie-mcp.local>
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] ui: add wasm display/input backend for emscripten builds

Adds ui/wasm.c (emscripten-only): XRGB8888 staging framebuffer exported
to JS (dirty-flag guarded), linux-keycode input via SPSC ring drained by
a bottom half, thread-safe wasm_quit(); adaptive dpy_refresh polling
(pmb887x LCD redraws via GraphicHwOps.gfx_update polls); extends
configs/meson/emscripten.txt link settings with ENV/HEAP exports and
EXIT_RUNTIME needed by the browser frontend.

Wasm-only by nature (a platform display backend, like sdl/gtk).  The
exported accessors are exactly what the page and the bench tooling use
(fb + key + quit + vclock + per-TB insn counters); the debug-only
exit-code histogram and cpu-halted probe of earlier revisions are gone.

Select with: qemu-system-arm ... -display wasm
